module gunbc.missing_mirror_admission_seed_growth

import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_model { RoadmapNodeId }
import gunbc.seed_growth { SeedGrowthJustification }

// Seed-growth obligation for the host-side copy of the missing-mirror admission -- the gate that
// decides whether a first mirror which is absent from the committed tree but present in the emit
// result is a surface this change is entitled to introduce, or an invented one. It is homed here,
// beside the obligation it declares, rather than inside gunbc.seed_growth_admission, which owns the
// roster and the join.

data missing_mirror_admission_seed_growth_justification: SeedGrowthJustification = SeedGrowthJustification {
  hand_authored_declarations: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.required_regen_host", decl_name: "MissingMirrorAuthority", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.required_regen_host", decl_name: "AdmittedMissingMirror", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.required_regen_host", decl_name: "MissingMirrorVerdict", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.required_regen_host", decl_name: "declared_partition_module_names", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.required_regen_host", decl_name: "declared_mirror_basename", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.required_regen_host", decl_name: "declared_modules_projecting_to", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.required_regen_host", decl_name: "missing_mirror_admission", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.required_regen_host", decl_name: "admitted_missing_mirrors", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.required_regen_host", decl_name: "PopulationVerdict", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.required_regen_host", decl_name: "AdmittedNewMirrorReceipt", field: WholeDeclaration }
  ],
  reason: "THE DECISION IS MODELED, AND THIS IS THE SECOND COPY OF IT -- stated plainly, because the alternative is a retained fork that reads as if it were an authority. The arms, their order, the refusal clauses and the derivation all live in v2.workflow.required_regen (MissingMirrorAuthority, MissingMirrorAdmission, missing_mirror_admission, declared_mirror_basename, declared_modules_projecting_to), and dag/test/claim/required_regen_admission_witness.dag witnesses that copy. The copy above is the one the merge gate EXECUTES, because the gate runs inside stage0, the crate that EMITS v2: it cannot call a v2-emitted realization of its own admission without a bootstrap cycle, and the interpreter route this file already uses (regen_scope_worktree_admitted) needs a wet evaluate over a subject this gate must decide BEFORE any tree is written. This copy is not the only one in the file, and the honest version of that sentence is the uncomfortable one: validate_compared_populations at :1849 classifies these very surfaces into the arms v2.workflow.required_regen declares as RegenSurfaceOutcome, whose own admission is required_regen_sync_admission at :519, and NO row declares that older pair. This row does not inherit that silence -- it declares its own half, and names the older undeclared copy as the follow-up it leaves behind rather than as precedent to copy. WHAT IS NOT DUPLICATED, and this is the part that would have been a fork: the spelling of a mirror name is not restated here. declared_mirror_basename is one call to the EMITTED mirror of gunbc.rust_emitted_edge::module_to_filename (src/v1/stage0/src/gunbc_rust_emitted_edge.rs:50), the fn the v1 emitters themselves use for file and path naming. The sibling rust_module_emit_filename is deliberately NOT used: its main-to-main_mod rule exists so an emitted module file does not collide with the crate entry file (dag/gunbc/rust_emitted_edge.dag:49-62), and a seed mirror is never the entry file, the crate root being lib.rs. SIBLINGS INSPECTED IN THIS FILE, with what was done: compared_mirror_rows at :12384 spelled the same fact by hand and now calls the same projection; :3268 spells a DIFFERENT fact (a crate directory from a package name, hyphens to underscores) and was left alone; :13379 spells it inside a test fixture builder, where it is input construction rather than a decision, and was left alone. WHAT THESE DECLARATIONS CARRY that the model cannot express from its own signature: reading the rows of the corpus THIS change carries (declared_partition_module_names over emitted_tree_packages, the single resolve of the run, with no fallback to the rows compiled into the running binary) and threading the admitted set through write, verify and manifest.",
  owning_dissolution_lane: "v1-hand-queue-drain" as RoadmapNodeId,
  trigger: "Delete MissingMirrorAuthority, AdmittedMissingMirror, MissingMirrorVerdict, declared_mirror_basename, declared_modules_projecting_to and missing_mirror_admission from this file and call a v2-emitted realization of the modeled admission instead, when a stage0 host can execute a .dag fold of this rule -- the capability the lane named in owning_dissolution_lane exists to deliver, and which regen_scope_worktree_admitted at :12903 in the same file already demonstrates from the other direction, calling into the interpreter rather than restating. WHAT DOES NOT RETIRE IT: re-modeling the arms again in .dag, which is where they already live; or moving the row-reading, which is host work by nature because it consumes the emitted tree of the running round.",
  current_boundary: "src/v1/stage0/src/required_regen_host.rs, the admission block: MissingMirrorAuthority :1697, AdmittedMissingMirror :1706, MissingMirrorVerdict :1714 with refusal_clause :1725, declared_partition_module_names :1749, declared_mirror_basename :1764, declared_modules_projecting_to :1774, missing_mirror_admission :1782, admitted_missing_mirrors :1810, PopulationVerdict :1837 with into_refusal :1844, and the receipt it feeds, AdmittedNewMirrorReceipt :1151. DRIFT GUARD, stated as a claim in the required lane rather than a promise: dag/test/claim/required_regen_admission_witness.dag now pins BOTH copies against the same facts -- every arm of the modeled decision by name, the spelling of each verdict on the host side, the host source calling the projection rather than spelling it, and the ABSENCE of the entry-file sibling from the host source -- so an arm renamed or dropped on either side reddens the gate. What that guard does NOT carry: behavioral equivalence beyond those spellings, which rests on the unit tests in this file and on the srv1 heal receipt recorded on the pull request."
}
